    "title": "COVID-19 cases increase in Louisiana; doctor suggests being tested - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ethan Goode ,\n1 hours ago\nBATON ROUGE, La. (Louisiana First) — COVID-19 cases are on the rise, and a new strain might hit harder than before.\n“We’ve always had a challenge here in Louisiana with COVID, even since the inception,” said My Doctors House owner Dr. Paulette Grey.\nIt’s no secret that Louisiana has battled some of the highest COVID-19 rates in the country, and more than five years after the first case, infections are on the rise again.\n“I think what we’re seeing now is probably a replication of what we saw in the beginning,” said Grey.\nGrey says students heading back to classrooms and dorms means we’ll see more coronavirus cases.\n“We know because COVID is a respiratory illness that the proximity or how close each person is to someone else has a lot to do with how the virus moves about,” said Grey.\nThe current strain has shown signs of more aggressive measures, reminding Grey and other doctors of earlier waves.\nGrey advises everyone to be tested right away. Protecting your own health has a bigger impact than you’d think.\n“I would implore people to really look to their health care providers as a trusted source and to really consider not only your individual health, but the public’s health as well,” said Grey.\nLatest News Copyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Louisiana First News.",
